   1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
   2: """fbpending DRAIN PROBE -- a RUNG-3 detector that MEASURES the pending-interrupt
   3: backlog of footbridge timer 1 in ~10 s, instead of waiting 43 s for it to overflow.
   4: 
   5: WHY THIS EXISTS.  The rung-3 witness (fbpending_witness.py) proves the defect by
   6: running until the counter wraps, which takes 42.95 s at cats' emulated_hz and cannot
   7: be made faster than 31.51 s on ANY machine (the delivery ceiling is
   8: TIMER_MAX_CATCHUP x TIMER_BASE_FREQUENCY = 68,157,440 increments per wall second, and
   9: timer_tick0 is called from nowhere else).  A gate row cannot spend that.
  10: 
  11: THE TRICK: MEASURE THE COUNTER, DO NOT WAIT FOR IT TO OVERFLOW.
  12: 
  13:   1. The guest arms timer 1 at a KNOWN SLOW rate.  cats' emulated_hz is 50,000,000 and
  14:      reload_timer_value() asks for emulated_hz / effective_cycles(load, ctrl, 1).  With
  15:      TIMER_FCLK_256 and load 256 that is 50e6 / (256*256) = 762.94 Hz.
  16:   2. It free-runs for T seconds.  Nothing acks, so the backlog is rate*T -- UNLESS the
  17:      device bounds it.
  18:   3. It then FREEZES the timer by writing TIMER_1_LOAD = 0x00FFFFFF while keeping
  19:      TIMER_FCLK_256: the rate falls to 50e6/(0xFFFFFF*256) = 0.0116 Hz, one tick per
  20:      86 s.  *** A LOAD WRITE DOES NOT CLEAR pending_timer_interrupts *** (only a
  21:      TIMER_x_CONTROL write WITHOUT TIMER_ENABLE does -- dev_footbridge.c, the
  22:      `pending_timer_interrupts[timer_nr] = 0` store in the `else` of `if (idata &
  23:      TIMER_ENABLE)`), so the
  24:      backlog survives the freeze.  That turns a moving quantity into a static one.
  25:   4. It then DRAINS AND COUNTS.  DEVICE_TICK writes timer_value = random() %
  26:      effective_cycles(load, ctrl, 0) whenever the backlog is > 0, and with load
  27:      0x00FFFFFF that modulus is 0xFFFFFF, so the produced value is in [0, 0xFFFFFE].
  28:      The guest writes the sentinel 0x00FFFFFF -- which the modulo CANNOT produce and
  29:      which survives TIMER_x_VALUE's own `idata & TIMER_MAX_VAL` mask -- and spins.  A
  30:      changed read means one tick was delivered; the guest then writes TIMER_1_CLEAR
  31:      (one decrement) and repeats.  When the spin budget expires with the sentinel
  32:      intact, the backlog is 0 and the number of decrements IS the backlog.
  33: 
  34:   The measured number is the whole verdict: pre-fix it is rate*T.  No wrap, no 43 s,
  35:   and the row reports a NUMBER rather than a boolean.
  36: 
  37:   *** POST-FIX IT IS **NOT** THE CAP, AND THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS PARAGRAPH SAID IT
  38:   WAS. ***  Measured by a pass-2 seat on ONE binary with ONE bound of 762: backlog 3 at
  39:   4 s, 100 at 46 s, 375 at 0.5 s.  Once the bound is first reached the number is a
  40:   MODULAR RESIDUE of the delivered tick count, not the bound itself.
  41: 
  42:   That is why `--expect-cap` is a one-sided `bD <= CAP` and CANNOT distinguish a bound
  43:   of 762 from one of 7: the quantity it tests is structurally <= the bound whatever the
  44:   bound is.  The rows that actually pin the bound's VALUE live in
  45:   regress/diff_fbpending_bound.c (R5, an equality against the timer's own rate, and R6,
  46:   which re-arms at a different rate) -- and they exist because a one-token mutant
  47:   (`freq / 100.0`) destroyed 99% of the guest's clock while passing this probe.
  48: 
  49: ARM X -- THE PLACEMENT DISCRIMINATOR, and the reason it is not merely a second run.
  50:   dev_footbridge.c never calls timer_remove() and never lowers the core frequency when
  51:   the guest DISABLES a timer: TIMER_x_CONTROL without TIMER_ENABLE zeroes the counter
  52:   once (the same `= 0` store) and leaves the struct timer running.  So timer_tickN keeps incrementing a
  53:   counter that DEVICE_TICK will never look at.  Arm X arms the timer, immediately
  54:   disables it, free-runs, re-enables (which does NOT clear the counter) and then
  55:   measures.  A non-zero result proves the counter accrues while the device is disabled
  56:   -- which is exactly the state in which a bound placed in DEVICE_TICK cannot run.
  57: 
  58: ARMS
  59:   D  enabled throughout.  Backlog after T seconds.
  60:   X  disabled during the accrual.  Backlog after T seconds.  Q1's discriminator.
  61:   T  negative control: MMU left on, so the footbridge is not mapped.  Must not return
  62:      the device's answers.  (machine_cats.c's boot page tables map only the low 256 MB;
  63:      the footbridge is at PA 0x42000000.)
  64:   K  failability control: arm D's prologue plus ONE instruction, a read of
  65:      IRQ_ENABLE_CLEAR (+0x18c, write-only per the DC21285), which dev_footbridge.c's
  66:      `case IRQ_ENABLE_CLEAR` read branch answers with fatal() then exit(1).  A probe in
  67:      which nothing can die proves nothing by surviving; K must die WITH its complaint AND
  68:      exit 1, and every surviving arm must reap exit 0.  #539 moved this from +0x188 (now
  69:      a readable register); the round that declines +0x18c retires the bridge.
  70: 
  71: Every RAM output word is poisoned with 0xDEADBEEF first and every verdict row requires
  72: the values it consults to be PRESENT.  Every planted instruction is checked, as it
  73: EXECUTES, against the emulator's own disassembly (the hand-assembled-encoding trap).
  74: 
  75: usage: fbpending_drain.py <gxemul-binary> <four-byte-raw-stub>
  76:                           [--accrue S] [--expect-cap N] [--learn]
  77: """
  78: import os, pty, re, select, signal, struct, sys, time
  79: 
  80: BIN = sys.argv[1]
  81: STUB = sys.argv[2]
  82: LEARN = "--learn" in sys.argv
  83: 
  84: 
  85: def _opt(name, default, cast):
  86:     if name in sys.argv:
  87:         return cast(sys.argv[sys.argv.index(name) + 1])
  88:     return default
  89: 
  90: 
  91: ACCRUE_S = _opt("--accrue", 4.0, float)
  92: EXPECT_CAP = _opt("--expect-cap", -1, int)   # -1 = report only
  93: #  WHICH of the four timers.  dev_footbridge.c derives timer_nr as
  94: #  (relative_addr >> 5) & 3, so timer N's registers sit at 0x300 + N*0x20 and
  95: #  TIMER_1_* is INDEX 0.  A fix applied to only one of the four callbacks passes a
  96: #  row that exercises only timer 1, which is why this is a parameter and not a
  97: #  constant.
  98: TIMER_NR = _opt("--timer", 0, int)
  99: TBASE = 0x300 + 0x20 * TIMER_NR
 100: T_LOAD, T_VALUE, T_CTRL, T_CLEAR = TBASE, TBASE + 4, TBASE + 8, TBASE + 12
 101: 
 102: CODE = 0x00008000
 103: DATA = 0x00009000
 104: FB = 0x42000000
 105: 
 106: EMU_HZ = 50000000.0
 107: #  --fast drives the counter at the machine's FULL emulated_hz (load 1, no
 108: #  prescaler = 50 MHz on cats), which is the only setting that reaches the 2^31
 109: #  wrap inside a run: 2^31 / 50e6 = 42.95 s.  The default 762.94 Hz would need
 110: #  32 days.  The freeze/drain machinery below is independent of the accrual rate.
 111: FAST = "--fast" in sys.argv
 112: LOAD_RUN = 0x001 if FAST else 0x100   # with FCLK_256 -> 50e6/65536 = 762.94 Hz
 113: LOAD_FREEZE = 0x00FFFFFF              # with FCLK_256 -> 0.0116 Hz
 114: CTRL_ON = 0x80 if FAST else 0x88      # TIMER_ENABLE [| TIMER_FCLK_256]
 115: CTRL_OFF = 0x00
 116: SENTINEL = 0x00FFFFFF                 # random() % 0xFFFFFF can never produce it
 117: SPIN = 0x00010000                     # 65536 iterations ~ 20 device-tick periods
 118: LIMIT = 200000
 119: RATE = EMU_HZ / (LOAD_RUN * (1.0 if FAST else 256.0))
 120: ONLY = _opt("--only", "", str)        # run a single arm, e.g. --only X
 121: 
 122: VENDOR = 0x1011
 123: LOADBACK = 0x00345678
 124: POISON = 0xDEADBEEF
 125: 
 126: # ---- RAM map (offsets from DATA) -----------------------------------------
 127: K_LIVE, K_SRC, K_L, K_FRZ, K_CON, K_SEN, K_SPIN, K_COFF = (
 128:     0x00, 0x04, 0x08, 0x0c, 0x10, 0x14, 0x18, 0x1c)
 129: O_DRAIN, O_ITER, O_LASTV, O_VEND, O_PHASE, K_LIM = (
 130:     0x20, 0x24, 0x28, 0x2c, 0x30, 0x34)
 131: 
 132: CONSTS = {K_LIVE: 0x11223344, K_SRC: 0x12345678, K_L: LOAD_RUN,
 133:           K_FRZ: LOAD_FREEZE, K_CON: CTRL_ON, K_SEN: SENTINEL,
 134:           K_SPIN: SPIN, K_COFF: CTRL_OFF, K_LIM: LIMIT}
 135: OUTS = (O_DRAIN, O_ITER, O_LASTV, O_VEND, O_PHASE)
 136: 
 137: R = dict(r0=0, r1=1, r2=2, r3=3, r4=4, r5=5, r6=6, r7=7, r8=8, r9=9,
 138:          sl=10, fp=11, ip=12, sp=13, lr=14, pc=15)
 139: 
 140: 
 141: # ---------------------------------------------------------------- assembler
 142: #  Encodings are GENERATED, not typed.  Every generated word is still checked
 143: #  against the emulator's own disassembly as it executes (arm E of the witness
 144: #  found this class of error four times in this project).
 145: def _imm12(v):
 146:     for rot in range(16):
 147:         c = ((v << (2 * rot)) | (v >> (32 - 2 * rot))) & 0xFFFFFFFF
 148:         if c < 256:
 149:             return (rot << 8) | c
 150:     raise ValueError("0x%x is not an ARM immediate" % v)
 151: 
 152: 
 153: def mov(rd, imm):
 154:     return 0xE3A00000 | (R[rd] << 12) | _imm12(imm), "mov %s,#0x%x" % (rd, imm)
 155: 
 156: 
 157: def movr(rd, rm):
 158:     return 0xE1A00000 | (R[rd] << 12) | R[rm], "mov %s,%s" % (rd, rm)
 159: 
 160: 
 161: def ldr(rd, rn, off):
 162:     return 0xE5900000 | (R[rn] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12) | off, \
 163:         "ldr %s,[%s,#%d]" % (rd, rn, off)
 164: 
 165: 
 166: def st(rd, rn, off):
 167:     return 0xE5800000 | (R[rn] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12) | off, \
 168:         "str %s,[%s,#%d]" % (rd, rn, off)
 169: 
 170: 
 171: def cmpr(rn, rm):
 172:     return 0xE1500000 | (R[rn] << 16) | R[rm], "cmps %s,%s" % (rn, rm)
 173: 
 174: 
 175: def subs1(rd):
 176:     return 0xE2500001 | (R[rd] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12), "subs %s,%s,#1" % (rd, rd)
 177: 
 178: 
 179: def add1(rd):
 180:     return 0xE2800001 | (R[rd] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12), "add %s,%s,#1" % (rd, rd)
 181: 
 182: 
 183: def br(cond, target, here):
 184:     off = ((target - here - 8) >> 2) & 0xFFFFFF
 185:     return (cond << 28) | 0x0A000000 | off, None
 186: 
 187: 
 188: NOP = (0xE1A00000, "mov r0,r0")
 189: 
 190: 
 191: def build(mmu_on=False, disable_during_accrual=False):
 192:     """Returns [(offset, word, expected_disassembly_or_None, comment)]."""
 193:     p = []
 194: 
 195:     def emit(off, wt, comment=""):
 196:         p.append((off, wt[0], wt[1], comment))
 197: 
 198:     if mmu_on:
 199:         for o in (0x00, 0x04, 0x08):
 200:             emit(o, NOP, "arm T: MMU LEFT ON -- the negative control")
 201:     else:
 202:         p.append((0x00, 0xEE110F10, "mrc 15,0,r0,cr1,cr0,0", "read CP15 c1"))
 203:         p.append((0x04, 0xE3C00001, "bic r0,r0,#1", "clear MMU enable"))
 204:         p.append((0x08, 0xEE010F10, "mcr 15,0,r0,cr1,cr0,0", "MMU OFF -> VA == PA"))
 205:     p.append((0x0c, 0xEE113F10, "mrc 15,0,r3,cr1,cr0,0", "C2: CP15 c1 read BACK"))
 206:     emit(0x10, mov("r0", FB), "footbridge base")
 207:     emit(0x14, mov("r4", DATA), "scratch RAM")
 208:     emit(0x18, ldr("r5", "r4", K_LIVE), "C1 liveness, expect 0x11223344")
 209:     emit(0x1c, ldr("r6", "r0", 0), "A1 VENDOR_ID, expect 0x1011")
 210:     emit(0x20, ldr("r2", "r4", K_SRC), "0x12345678 out of RAM")
 211:     emit(0x24, st("r2", "r0", T_LOAD), "TIMER_x_LOAD <- 0x12345678")
 212:     emit(0x28, ldr("r7", "r0", T_LOAD), "A2 expect 0x00345678 (the handler's mask)")
 213:     emit(0x2c, ldr("r2", "r4", K_CON), "CTRL = TIMER_ENABLE|TIMER_FCLK_256")
 214:     emit(0x30, st("r2", "r0", T_CTRL), "TIMER_1_CONTROL <- 0x88")
 215:     emit(0x34, ldr("r2", "r4", K_L), "load 256")
 216:     emit(0x38, st("r2", "r0", T_LOAD), "TIMER_1_LOAD <- 256 => 762.94 Hz")
 217:     emit(0x3c, ldr("r8", "r4", K_SEN), "sentinel 0x00FFFFFF")
 218:     emit(0x40, ldr("ip", "r4", K_SPIN), "spin budget")
 219:     emit(0x44, mov("sl", 0), "drained count")
 220:     emit(0x48, mov("lr", 0), "accrual iterations")
 221:     emit(0x4c, mov("r1", 0), "")
 222:     emit(0x50, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 0")
 223:     if disable_during_accrual:
 224:         emit(0x54, ldr("r2", "r4", K_COFF), "arm X: CTRL = 0")
 225:         emit(0x58, st("r2", "r0", T_CTRL),
 226:              "arm X: DISABLE.  Zeroes the counter ONCE and leaves the core timer running.")
 227:     else:
 228:         emit(0x54, NOP, "")
 229:         emit(0x58, NOP, "")
 230:     #  accrual loop -- publishes liveness and a fresh VENDOR_ID every iteration
 231:     emit(0x5c, add1("lr"), "ACCRUE: iterations++")
 232:     emit(0x60, st("lr", "r4", O_ITER), "publish iterations")
 233:     emit(0x64, ldr("r1", "r0", 0), "fresh VENDOR_ID read, every iteration")
 234:     emit(0x68, st("r1", "r4", O_VEND), "publish it")
 235:     p.append((0x6c, br(0xE, CODE + 0x5c, CODE + 0x6c)[0], None, "b ACCRUE"))
 236:     #  ---- DRAIN entry.  The harness sets pc here after the accrual free-run. ----
 237:     if disable_during_accrual:
 238:         emit(0x70, ldr("r2", "r4", K_CON), "arm X: re-enable")
 239:         emit(0x74, st("r2", "r0", T_CTRL),
 240:              "arm X: CONTROL <- 0x88.  reload_timer_value() does NOT clear the counter.")
 241:     else:
 242:         emit(0x70, NOP, "")
 243:         emit(0x74, NOP, "")
 244:     emit(0x78, ldr("r2", "r4", K_FRZ), "0x00FFFFFF")
 245:     emit(0x7c, st("r2", "r0", T_LOAD), "FREEZE: LOAD <- 0x00FFFFFF => 0.0116 Hz")
 246:     emit(0x80, mov("r1", 1), "")
 247:     emit(0x84, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 1")
 248:     emit(0x88, ldr("sp", "r4", K_LIM), "drain limit")
 249:     emit(0x8c, st("r8", "r0", T_VALUE), "DLOOP: TIMER_1_VALUE <- sentinel")
 250:     emit(0x90, movr("fp", "ip"), "reset spin budget")
 251:     emit(0x94, ldr("r9", "r0", T_VALUE), "SPIN: read TIMER_1_VALUE")
 252:     emit(0x98, cmpr("r9", "r8"), "")
 253:     p.append((0x9c, br(0x1, CODE + 0xac, CODE + 0x9c)[0], None, "bne TICKSEEN"))
 254:     emit(0xa0, subs1("fp"), "")
 255:     p.append((0xa4, br(0x1, CODE + 0x94, CODE + 0xa4)[0], None, "bne SPIN"))
 256:     p.append((0xa8, br(0xE, CODE + 0xc8, CODE + 0xa8)[0], None,
 257:               "budget expired, sentinel intact -> backlog is 0"))
 258:     emit(0xac, st("r9", "r4", O_LASTV), "TICKSEEN: publish the value the tick wrote")
 259:     emit(0xb0, st("r1", "r0", T_CLEAR), "TIMER_1_CLEAR -- one decrement")
 260:     emit(0xb4, add1("sl"), "")
 261:     emit(0xb8, st("sl", "r4", O_DRAIN), "publish the drained count")
 262:     emit(0xbc, cmpr("sl", "sp"), "")
 263:     p.append((0xc0, br(0xA, CODE + 0xdc, CODE + 0xc0)[0], None, "bge OVER"))
 264:     p.append((0xc4, br(0xE, CODE + 0x8c, CODE + 0xc4)[0], None, "b DLOOP"))
 265:     emit(0xc8, mov("r1", 3), "DONE:")
 266:     emit(0xcc, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 3")
 267:     emit(0xd0, ldr("r1", "r0", 0), "final VENDOR_ID")
 268:     emit(0xd4, st("r1", "r4", O_VEND), "")
 269:     p.append((0xd8, br(0xE, CODE + 0xd8, CODE + 0xd8)[0], None, "HALT"))
 270:     emit(0xdc, mov("r1", 4), "OVER:")
 271:     emit(0xe0, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 4 -- drain limit hit")
 272:     p.append((0xe4, br(0xE, CODE + 0xd8, CODE + 0xe4)[0], None, "b HALT"))
 273:     return p
 274: 
 275: 
 276: DRAIN_ENTRY = CODE + 0x70
 277: PROLOGUE_N = 21          # 0x00 .. 0x50 inclusive
