 541: #  *** EXTENDED 2026-08-20 FOR THE METHOD FORM, and narrowly on purpose given the history
 542: #  in the paragraph above. ***  Every probe until now wrote `send()` as a closure over a local
 543: #  `buf`, so the guard read `return wait(mark=_mark, ...)`.  fbpending_drain_probe.py is the
 544: #  first CLASS-BASED probe in the tree: its guard is `return self.wait(mark=_mark, ..., 
 545: #  timeout=timeout)`, which is not a spelling variation but a different construct, and the
 546: #  pattern could not see it AT ALL -- the guard was present, correct, and uncounted.
 547: #
 548: #  That is a wider blind spot than the `mark`/`_mark` one filed as sh4markspell: a whole probe
 549: #  STYLE was invisible.  The two additions here are `\(self\.\)\?` and an optional trailing
 550: #  argument.  Both are anchored -- `mark=_mark` and the full `echo=` conditional still have to
 551: #  be present and in order -- so neither re-opens the hole the three earlier tightenings closed:
 552: #  a site that passes the argument, or drops the conditional, still fails to match.
 553: conv_mark=$(probe_code 'return \(self\.\)\?wait(mark=_mark, echo=[a-z][a-z]* if [a-z][a-z]* else None[,)]' | grep -c .)
